Article 5 (Working-Level Support Group)
(1) A working-level support group shall be established within the National Court Administration to support the activities of the Committee. <Amended on September 6, 2016.>
(2) The head and secretary of the working-level support group shall be designated by the Minister of the National Court Administration from among judges and court officials. <Amended on September 6, 2016.>
(3) The Committee may have the head, members and secretary of the working-level support group attend Committee meetings to express opinions and provide explanations. <Newly Inserted on September 6, 2016.>
(4) The duties of the working-level support group shall be to support the activities of the Committee as follows: <Newly Inserted on September 6, 2016.>
1. Matters concerning the recommendation and commissioning, etc. of candidates for persons involved in insolvency proceedings, including custodial committee members, custodians, examiners, bankruptcy trustees and rehabilitation commissioners (excluding rehabilitation commissioners under Article 601 (1) 2 of the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act);
2. Regular and occasional evaluations of the work performed by persons specified in subparagraph 1;
3. Matters concerning the operation of meetings, including the preparation and distribution of agenda items;
4. External cooperation, education, publicity and publication of materials;
5. Other matters necessary for the duties of the Committee.
